From f319062f247af718e2b8621d8cccd4a13d44c7b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mauro Carvalho Chehab <mchehab+huawei@kernel.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:35:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mce-intel-sb: properly check rank0 and rank1

Coverity reports two issues there:

1.  CID 1685832: (#1 of 1): Logically dead code (DEADCODE)
	dead_error_line: Execution cannot reach this statement: if (rank0 >= 0U) do { ....

2.  CID 1685833: (#1 of 1): Unsigned compared against 0 (NO_EFFECT)
	unsigned_compare: This greater-than-or-equal-to-zero comparison of an unsigned value is always true. rank0 >= 0U.

Both are because the logic sets rank0 and rank1 to -1 and then
check later.

Change the types to integer, allowing the tests to check if the
retrieved register values are ok.

Signed-off-by: Mauro Carvalho Chehab <mchehab+huawei@kernel.org>
---
 events-arch-x86/mce-intel-sb.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/events-arch-x86/mce-intel-sb.c b/events-arch-x86/mce-intel-sb.c
index 883751e..b46ac31 100644
--- a/events-arch-x86/mce-intel-sb.c
+++ b/events-arch-x86/mce-intel-sb.c
@@ -70,7 +70,8 @@ void snb_decode_model(struct ras_events *ras, struct mce_event *e)
 {
 	struct mce_priv *mce = ras->mce_priv;
 	uint32_t mca = e->status & 0xffff;
-	unsigned int rank0 = -1, rank1 = -1, chan;
+	int rank0 = -1, rank1 = -1;
+	unsigned int chan;
 
 	switch (e->bank) {
 	case 4:
